  "window": "Nov. 11–12, 2026",
  "summary": "A Nenana traffic stop on Nov. 11 ended in a court summons for driving with a revoked license, the only new Interior police or trooper record since the previous edition. As of about 5 a.m. on Nov. 12 neither the Alaska State Troopers nor Fairbanks police had posted any Fairbanks-area item for that date, and no criminal case had been opened at the Fairbanks, Nenana, Healy or Delta Junction courthouses since the afternoon of Nov. 11. In the Fairbanks arson case filed Nov. 11 the court record shows the arraignment was continued, with a further arraignment set for Nov. 12 and preliminary hearings for Nov. 19 and Dec. 1. The filing counts below are the Alaska Court System weekly charges report's own counts for its window of Nov. 5 to Nov. 11.",
  "commentary": null,
