      "severity": "felony",
      "cases": [
        "4FA-26-02272CR"
      ],
      "title": "Arson case hearings set: Keith Richardson",
      "body": [
        "Keith Richardson, 40, of Fairbanks is charged with arson in the first degree — damaging property by fire and putting someone in danger of serious injury — a Class A felony, punishable by up to 20 years, and with criminal trespass in the first degree, entering or staying on land intending to commit a crime, a Class A misdemeanor. Neither count is recorded as domestic violence related.",
        "The court record shows the arraignment held Nov. 11 was continued. A further arraignment is set for Nov. 12 and preliminary hearings for Nov. 19 and Dec. 1. He is represented by the Public Defender Agency.",
        "Case 4FA-26-02272CR. Troopers say the charges arise from an improvised incendiary device thrown through the window of an occupied Fairbanks house early on Nov. 11."
      ],
